      "description": "Commercial building in Windsor",
      "extract": "The Crooked House of Windsor is a commercial building in Windsor, England, dating from c. 1687. It is the oldest teahouse in England and Grade II listed. The building was reconstructed in the 17th century and now stands on \"an outrageous slant.\" It has three storeys and bay windows to the front and rear.",
